{"chunk_id": "d782a8d7ac1b", "text": "Satyavati urges the sage Vyasa\u2014her son by the sage Parashara\u2014to preserve the Kuru dynasty after King Vichitravirya dies childless, leaving two widows. She argues that both parents share authority over children and appeals to duty, lineage, and the welfare of the kingdom, asking Vyasa to father heirs through the widowed queens according to the ancient custom of niyoga. Vyasa agrees, though he warns that the women must endure his harsh ascetic appearance. When the princess Ambika is sent to him, she becomes terrified by his grim, wild form and shuts her eyes during their union. Vyasa later prophesies that her son will be mighty and wise but blind because of her fear. This child will be born as Dhritarashtra, foreshadowing future tensions in the Kuru line.\nSatyavati arranges for Vyasa to impregnate Ambika to continue the Kuru line; frightened by his appearance, she closes her eyes, leading to the birth of the blind Dhritarashtra.\nThemes: dynastic succession, niyoga practice, fear and consequence, maternal authority, fate of heirs", "vector": [0.011036349460482597, -0.023305734619498253, -0.013610820285975933, -0.0016861088806763291, -0.0059991939924657345, 0.030297454446554184, -0.005287827458232641, -0.010426606051623821, -0.014918380416929722, -0.016788259148597717, 0.02337348461151123, -0.007127218879759312, 0.020839663222432137, 0.014837081544101238, -0.02478266879916191, 0.010562105104327202, 0.04482289031147957, -0.004583235364407301, 0.03482310473918915, -0.020528016611933708, -0.01314335037022829, 0.004169965162873268, -0.005989031866192818, 0.013299173675477505, -0.02907796949148178, 0.02242499403655529, 0.011835790239274502, -0.022601142525672913, 0.0036279712803661823, -0.015528122894465923, -0.020514465868473053, 0.002159506781026721, 0.0188071858137846, -0.03574449196457863, -0.02337348461151123, -0.0027878808323293924, -0.0050879670307040215, -0.010656953789293766, 0.02043316699564457, -0.01190353929996490